      "writtenOn": "2025-11-07T21:17:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMO it\u0027s fine to add an assert since it won\u0027t change the behavior in non-crashing cases. We actually used to have bounds checks in some of our ityp containers too but took them out because libc++ is configured to do them for us. https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/260462\n\nIt seems like C\u0027s `assert` can be used in constexpr, but I don\u0027t know if it\u0027s possible to make ours work. It would be very nice though.\n\nMaybe we can do something like, `if (std::is_constant_evaluated())` to choose between DAWN_ASSERT and some kind of compile-time failure? (best I can find for that is to throw an exception, idk if that works for us)",
